    11	## 0. Conventions
    12	
    13	* Spin f, D = 2f+1, bosons a_m (m = −f..f), Condon–Shortley phases. Pair operator
    14	  P† = Σ_m (−1)^m a†_m a†_{−m}; [P, P†] = 4N̂ + 2D. The seniority-v states are the harmonic
    15	  (Pψ = 0) states. |N v α L M⟩ = (P†)^n h_{vαLM}/‖·‖ with N = v + 2n and h harmonic of degree v.
    16	* One-body CFP: |N; vαL M⟩ = Σ c(NvαL; N−1 v'α'L') [χ(N) ⊗ |N−1; v'α'L'⟩]_{LM}, with the particle
    17	  coupled first, ⟨f m; L' M'|L M⟩. In second quantization,
    18	  c = ⟨N vαL L| a†_μ |N−1 v'α'L' L'⟩ / (√N ⟨f μ; L' L'|L L⟩), μ = L − L'. The reduced CFP is
    19	  r(vαL; v−1 α'L') := c at N = v, so Σ_{α'L'} r² = 1.
    20	* Spin 2: α is the Chacón–Moshinsky–Sharp label e = n_Δ (number of SO(3)-scalar trios), with
    21	  λ = v − 3e. Basis states are harmonic projections of covariant monomials f^a H^b T^c j^e of the
    22	  binary quartic. Here f = a†_2, H is the spin-2 pair, T the spin-3 trio and j the scalar trio,
    23	  with a = L − λ, c = (2λ − L) mod 2 and b = (2λ − L − 3c)/2. In a multiplicity block they are
    24	  Gram–Schmidt orthonormalized, either "asc" (e = 0 first; compare Caprio–Rowe–Welsh, who
    25	  orthonormalize their monomials in order of increasing t — we did not check that their monomials
