   167	## C. Spin 2: top families L = 2v − k, k ≤ 8, as rational functions of v
   168	
   169	The deficit method of §B is extended with the harmonic projection
   170	H(φ) = Σ_i β_i (P†)^i P^i φ, β_i = (−1)^i/(2^i i! Π_{l≤i}(D+2v−2−2l)). P acts on the implicit z₂
   171	power through a factor v − |d|. The covariant monomial H^b T^c j^e is fixed in deficit coordinates,
   172	and f^a only fixes the degree. The basis vectors are checked symbolically: S₊ψ = 0 and Pψ = 0
   173	identically in v. Integer roots of the norms, of the CG factors and of the overlaps are checked so
   174	that no excluded v lies in the stated range.
   175	
   176	* **k ≤ 5 (multiplicity-free).** All 14 transitions are products of linear factors, for example
   177	  r²(k=4→4) = (v−4)(2v−3)(2v−1)(4v−5)(4v−3)/(v(2v−5)(2v+1)(4v−9)(4v−7)). The full list is in
   178	  [results/spin2_top_families_k8_asc.txt](results/spin2_top_families_k8_asc.txt). **Reproduction:**
   179	  with τ = v − 1, all 14 nonzero squared entries of Table III of Pan, Bao, Zhang, Draayer (2014)
   180	  are reproduced exactly; signs differ by phase convention.
   181	* **k = 6 (multiplicity 2).** In the asc basis the formulas contain the irreducible quartic
   182	  128v⁴−1376v³+5608v²−10042v+6465 = 2304(2v+1)·q(φ₀). The basis-independent total parentage
   183	  weight into the k' = 2 daughter is Q_{dd} = 3·F(v)/(v(v−2)(2v−5)(2v+1)(4v−11)(4v−9)) with
   184	  F(v) = 32v⁴−288v³+1024v²−1692v+1065. F(τ+1) is exactly Pan et al.'s f(τ+1). Their Table IV
   185	  basis is the **principal-parent basis of the k' = 2 daughter** (χ = 2) and its orthogonal
   186	  complement (χ = 1). All 8 multiplicity-free rows of their Table IV are **reproduced exactly**
   187	  from basis-independent data (`$PY compare_pan2014.py`: `Table III: 14/14 squared entries
   188	  reproduced exactly; Table IV (multiplicity-free rows): 8/8 reproduced`). In the
   189	  **trio-first (desc) basis** every k = 6 CFP into a multiplicity-free daughter
   190	  has the form (rational)²·(product of linear factors)/q₂(v), with the **irreducible quadratic**
